    {
      "id": "CO-ING-6-2026-W05-family-members-001-MASTERY-v4",
      "statement": "\"Carlos has a brother. ___ name is Andrés.\"",
      "context": "In Barranquilla, students practice possessive adjectives.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "His",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correcto. \"His\" para posesión de un hombre (Carlos)."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Her",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrecto. \"Her\" es para posesión de una mujer."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "My",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrecto. \"My\" es para primera persona."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Your",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrecto. \"Your\" es para segunda persona."
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "A",
      "explanation": "Possessive adjectives: my (mi), your (tu/su), his (su de él), her (su de ella), its (su de cosa/animal), our (nuestro), their (su de ellos).\r\n\r\n---",
